  "adapter_notes": [
    "The helpers are copied verbatim; source and function SHA-256 fingerprints pin the inspected implementation, not only legacy version labels.",
    "Adapters use ISO date comparisons, require explicit frozen windows/clock compatibility/missing-stat disposition and preserve unknown availability.",
    "P1 discovery thresholds and chronological stability rules and P2 standard/252 thresholds are retained. P2 missing-stat behavior remains legacy_failed_v1, pending a production policy disposition.",
    "P2 interval scheduling is the same maximum non-overlapping interval algorithm on validated date strings with shared boundaries allowed; fixed CS requires same target endpoint per date.",
    "No legacy writers, registry imports, dynamic source path, scientific data, or results are imported."
  ]
